 "about": {
  "numbers": "Limits, defaults, durations, percentages and prices. Use `tables` on Quotas, the storage class comparison table, the retrieval options table and the Glacier comparison table; quote a limit as the row plus header_text.",
  "behavior": "Can / cannot / only / by default rules: versioning, Object Lock, replication, encryption, lifecycle, access control, presigned URLs, events.",
  "decisions": "Comparisons and trade-offs the exam hinges on (storage class ladder, encryption options, presigned vs CloudFront, Transfer Acceleration vs CloudFront vs multipart, S3 vs EBS vs EFS, Object Lock vs MFA delete), pricing dimensions, Callvale's decision facts and the two case studies.",
  "faq": "Quick-fire items with verbatim FAQ answers from www/s3/faqs (saa.py faq ... --find). One row per item of kind faq, plus any demand item tagged faq.",
  "changes": "Each FRESHNESS hypothesis re-grounded: the dated row in WhatsNew or document-history (quote the row) plus the current page that states the new value. Mark GA after 2026-07-15 as not examinable yet."
 },
